{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry you missed the Q4 planning invite. I checked and it isn't stuck in your spam quarantine, and your mailbox has plenty of space, so neither of those is the cause. Could you help with a few quick things? 1) Sign in to Outlook on the web and see whether the invite or meeting shows up there, even if it's missing from the Outlook app on your laptop. 2) Tell me if anyone, such as an assistant, has delegate access to your calendar. If so, the invite may have gone only to them. 3) Ask the meeting organizer to send the invite to you again, and let me know who the organizer is. Please also tell me if invites from this person have been missing before. If the resent invite still doesn't arrive, reply here and we'll look into it further.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket: user didn't get the Q4 planning invite that others got. Followed KB-012 quick checks. lookup_user: account active, no lockout, mailbox 27.9% used (not a quota problem). Spam quarantine: empty, so the invite wasn't quarantined. No tool available to check delegates, so I asked the user. I also asked her to compare Outlook on the web with the desktop app (KB-009 if only the desktop app is wrong) and to ask the organizer to resend. Escalate to Tier 2 per KB-012 if invites from this one internal organizer never arrive (possible mail rule or transport issue).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-012"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
